   "id": "syn-mu-1",
   "text": "Micron Technology returned to profit in its latest quarter as prices for memory chips rebounded and demand from data centre customers for high-bandwidth memory used in AI systems outstripped supply.\n\nThe company said its high-bandwidth memory output for the year was sold out and that it had begun pricing contracts for the next year. Revenue rose strongly from the prior quarter and gross margin turned positive after several quarters of losses.\n\nThe chief executive said the memory industry's supply discipline, with producers holding back capacity additions, had helped prices recover faster than expected. Micron raised its capital spending plan to expand production of advanced memory.\n\nShares rose in after-hours trading. Analysts said the forecast for the coming quarter implied further margin expansion, though the memory market remains cyclical and consumer device demand is still soft.",
   "context": "article",
